// lset: the generic "store into a list element" helper (an imported list
// can't be index-assigned directly, but passing it as a parameter makes the
// lvalue an identifier again; lists are reference-semantic so the store is
// shared -- see demos/moonbuggy/engine/core/core-1/cell/cell.id).
//
// rng_range/noise_range build on rng_next() (rng2.id) for everything the
// galaxy generator needs: rng_range(n) is a uniform pick in 0..n-1;
// noise_range(half) is symmetric jitter in -half..+half, used for angle,
// height and color noise alike (particles/shape/theta.id,
// particles/look/position/y.id, particles/look/color/tint.id).

lset(int[] xs, int i, int v) {
  xs[i] = v;
} return void;

rng_range(int n) {
} return int rng_next() % n;

noise_range(int half) {
  int span = 2 * half + 1;
} return int rng_range(span) - half;
